# tally 2.3.1 R3, N245.9 (E §11 REQ-CLOCK, a literal cut after on in any form): an `as if {known D}` with a
# literal D after on in an ask's line refuses the request, the run's one result. Before: q10's line
# RUN-DOMAIN, the other asks answered.
=== lawclock.tally
model lawpin
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input w: date
input rate: money PLN

def cost: money PLN at reader
  rule one = rate

ask q8: cost as if {known 2026-03-01} law 2026-03-01
ask q10: (cost as if {known 2026-09-01}) + cost law 2026-03-01


version v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-06-30
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 10.00 PLN "s"

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 20.00 PLN "s"

version v3
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = 2026-02-01 "s"
=== expect
refused: REQ-CLOCK known 2026-09-01 is after the model's on 2026-06-30
